GL renderer: stop paying the internal scale squared for mask rebuilds and reads.

Two things the GL backend did at full-surface size, or while waiting for the
GPU, independent of how much of the frame actually needed it. Both cost
grows with the internal scale S squared, which is the shape of the one 5x
measurement on record (60 FPS: 2,580 presents for 3,823 VBlanks at 5x, clean
at 2x; frame_perf at 5x: scene GPU 13.8 ms of a 16.7 ms frame).

1. Mask stencil rebuild, scissored.
   Opaque and dual-source textured batches without set-mask skip their
   stencil encoding (alpha is exact; the stencil copy is only needed once the
   game turns mask CHECKING on). When it does, rebuild_mask_stencils
   re-derived the stencil from alpha over the whole 1024S x 512S surface and
   again over every native-wide surface: a blit plus a full-screen stencil
   draw, per surface, per E6h check-on edge. At 5x that is 13 Mpx twice per
   surface, for a drawn band of 320x240 (1.9 Mpx at 5x).
   Now each such batch adds its vertex bbox (one pixel of guard, clipped to
   the draw area it is scissored to) to s_stencil_dirty, and the rebuild
   blits and redraws only that rect on the hr surface, and the same rows at
   full width on the wide surfaces (the mirror moves X - the backdrop stretch
   can reach any column - but never Y, and uses the same Y scissor). An unset
   rect with the stencil invalid still means everything, as before.

2. Guest VRAM reads wait for the GPU only when they need to.
   glb_vram_transfer_out (GP0 C0h / DMA from VRAM) and glb_vram_read went
   through ensure_cpu whenever ANY pixel had been drawn by the GPU since the
   last readback: flush, pack, and a synchronous glReadPixels that waits for
   everything queued - the frame's GPU time, paid on the emulation thread.
   s_gpu_dirty is now backed by a 16x8 map of 64x64-pixel tiles, marked by
   every GPU write to canonical VRAM (prims, fills incl. wrapped segments,
   copies; one pixel of guard) and cleared with it. A read whose rect
   (wrapping like the PS1) touches no GPU-written tile is served from s_vram,
   which is exact there because CPU uploads land in it first; otherwise it
   reads back exactly as before. Whole-VRAM consumers (display render,
   screenshots, 24-bit scanout, shutdown) are unchanged. The heartbeat's
   gl.sync_skips counts the reads that no longer wait.

Also, opt-in for A/B only: PSX_GL_SEMI_BATCH=1 lets consecutive dual-source
semi-transparent textured prims (modes 0/1/3, mask check off) share one draw
instead of one draw each. Fixed-function blending inside a draw is applied in
primitive order and each fragment chooses opaque vs blended itself, so only
opaque/semi interleaving needs the split, which the batch key already makes.
Default off until gl.semi_isolated and a visual check justify it.

Not changed: the hold-last copy of the drawable on every present is window
sized (2560x1440 = 3.7 Mpx), not scaled by S.

No file here is in codegen_hash_sources.cmake; overlay shards are unaffected.

